# studies-archive-method-ab-2026

> An A/B of the expected-value against the sampled forward on one event. It rebuilds
> `DetectorParams.from_flat` from 8 scalars in order to resize `qe_corrections`, which **resets** TTS,
> the per-PMT gains, angular reflection and scintillation to their defaults — so it compares more than
> the flag it names — and `temperature` changes with the flag the comment claims is isolated. If you
> revive it, use `load_detector_params(path, num_sensors=N)`, which already does the resize.

## What is in this tarball

| path | size at `eaf2e89f` | what it does |
|---|---|---|
| `scripts/compare_method_ab.py` | 6.1 KB, 153 lines | For each source position, draws `n_trials` independent runs at fixed `n_photons` in both propagator modes and reports total-detected-charge mean and σ, the per-sensor mean ratio B/A (≈1 if unbiased), the per-sensor σ ratio on illuminated sensors, and "equivalent photons" `N · var_A/var_B` |

`load_detector_params` is at `lucid/detector_params.py:600` and its second
parameter is `num_sensors: int = None`, so the one line this study needed
already existed when it was written.

## The two defects, quoted

**1. It compares more than the flag it names.** `:108-117` builds the detector
parameters from eight scalars:

```python
dp = DetectorParams.from_flat(
    num_sensors=N_sensors,
    scatter_length=…, mie_scatter_length=…, g=…,
    wall_reflection_rate=…, sensor_reflection_rate=…,
    absorption_length=…, qe=…,
    qe_corrections=jnp.ones(N_sensors),
)
```

Everything the physics config carried and `from_flat` does not take — TTS, the
per-PMT gains, the angular reflection parameters and scintillation — silently
reverts to its library default. Both arms get the same defaults, so the A/B is
internally consistent; what it is **not** is an A/B at the configuration named
on the command line.

**2. `temperature` moves with the flag the comment says is isolated.** The
comment at `:75-76` reads "Varying only `use_expected_value` isolates the
propagator." Seven lines later, `:82`:

```python
temperature=None if not use_expected_value else 0.2,
```

So the sampled arm runs the hard-step overlap (`None`) and the
expected-value arm runs a soft kernel at 0.2. Whatever difference the script
measures is the propagator mode **and** the overlap softness together, and the
comment asserts the opposite. (In the house naming standard this knob is
`overlap_sigma_frac`, dimensionless, σ as a fraction of the sensor radius —
`temperature` is the old spelling that meant two unrelated things.)

## Caller check at `eaf2e89f`

Nobody. No import of `scripts.compare_method_ab` or `compare_method_ab`
anywhere in `lucid/`, `tests/`, `examples/`, `analysis/`, `tutorials/`, any
`*.sh`/`*.sbatch`, or `pyproject.toml`'s `[project.scripts]`. The only mention
in the tree was its own row in `scripts/README.md`.

## If you want this comparison

Ask it as a test, not as a script: fix the detector parameters once with
`load_detector_params(path, num_sensors=N)`, hold the overlap knob fixed across
both arms, and assert the per-sensor mean ratio against 1 with a tolerance set
by the trial count. That is three assertions, and it would have caught both
defects above.
